@ [derivation] continuation of the user-authorized five-hour Cantor production slice after exact Slice9 closure

& [Intent]
  + make Slice9 useful inside an inference tool loop by allowing one complete lifecycle request to be registered once and later validated through its compact exact handle
  + keep this as a separate volatile MCP process rather than changing the closed stateless Slice8 server
  + use the existing pure immutable Slice9 registry as the semantic owner and let the adapter own only synchronized process-local custody

& [ToolSurface]
  + expose one closed tool route with tagged REGISTER VALIDATE and INSPECT commands so the inference primer loads one bounded schema
  + REGISTER accepts one complete strict NativeLifecycleValidationRequest and returns its exact handle plus current registry summary
  + VALIDATE accepts one exact handle resolves retained meaning and returns the unchanged Slice7 lifecycle response plus registry summary
  + INSPECT returns bounded registry count retained-byte and root-digest metadata without returning retained request bodies

& [State]
  + one server process starts with one empty Slice9 registry and serializes commands through one async mutex
  + successful registration atomically replaces the current immutable registry value with its validated successor
  + every refusal leaves the current registry byte-identical
  + restart loses all entries and stale handles then refuse visibly

& [Bounds]
  + retain Slice9 limits of eight entries eight megabytes per request and sixty-four megabytes aggregate
  + measure complete MCP arguments before typed decoding against the core request ceiling plus a bounded wrapper allowance
  + bound fault and text summaries and keep structuredContent as the complete machine response

& [Honesty]
  + successful registration means exact volatile retention only
  + successful validation means the retained request was replayed by Slice7 and preserves artifact_valid verification_valid lifecycle_refused or input_refused exactly
  + digest lookup does not reconstruct omitted meaning and registry coherence is not truth correctness safety authentication authorization signature permission or effect authority

& [Security]
  + deny unknown fields commands and methods and refuse malformed oversized duplicate missing substituted or corrupted identities without partial mutation
  + the adapter stores no secrets and performs no filesystem network provider model runner signing admission installation deployment execution or other external effect
  + this process-local P0 provides no client isolation authentication durable persistence expiry eviction crash recovery or multi-process concurrency claim

& [Acceptance]
  + direct REGISTER then compact VALIDATE equals direct Slice7 validation for valid and refused retained requests
  + INSPECT never discloses retained request bodies
  + duplicate missing malformed oversized unknown method restart and concurrent equal registration cases fail closed with exact state accounting
  + official rmcp subprocess client lists one tool performs register inspect validate and sees restart loss
  + focused debug optimized release lint format evidence and diff gates pass without weakening host security policy

& [Locked]
  + Slice7 semantics Slice8 stateless behavior durable storage authentication authorization multi-client identity eviction expiry provider model process runner filesystem network signing admission installation deployment execution internal llama.cpp FPGA remote OneDrive EVO-X2 and Minecraft
